  "problem": "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. $\\mu \\cdot \\sigma -\\text{min}({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{16})$\n\nII. $\\mu -\\text{median}({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{16})$\n\nIII. $\\sigma -max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{15})$",
